      "kind": "transition",
      "result": "PASS",
      "disposition_reason": "On Production, a blank name and a one-space name both draw Required under Name and leave port 5432. The space keeps the caret column of the one-character name. Ports 65536, abc, and 0 draw Port must\u2026 (U+2026). The validator in connections.rs returns Port must be 1\u201365535; reveal::fit clips that string in the port column at 120\u00d740. Submit sets the status Fix the highlighted fields, leaves Edit connection open, and leaves Production in the tree. Connection saved is absent. The 120\u00d740 checkpoint is that frame with a blank name, port 0, both drawn errors, host prod-db-1.acme.io, database acme_prod, and username acme_ops. At 80\u00d724 the same form is a drawer, so the tree is covered. Name is blank with Required, the port is 0, and the port error is clipped to Port mus\u2026 (U+2026). The status Fix the highlighted fields is on the footer and Connection saved is absent. After the reopen shots, Ctrl+S with port 65535 saves. The detail shows Production, prod-db-1.acme.io:65535, Engine PostgreSQL, Environment production, and Safe Mode with deliberate acknowledgement. Opening Edit again shows name Production and port 65535.",
      "reference_commit": "fffe002e936d3621f22f9132144066a1374d5d74",
      "execution_commit": "89263a012c376b8d5edc17a46678762e1a381977",
      "evidence_paths": [],
